    "homepage": "https://conicplex.com/plugins/plexblocks-carousel-slider-for-block-editor/",
    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Carousel Slider for Gutenberg Block Editor adds a practical slider block for image carousels, feature slides, marketing sections, and rotating content layouts.</p>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>slide management in the block editor</li>\n<li>responsive slide layouts</li>\n<li>arrows, dots, autoplay, and loop options</li>\n<li>support for image and content-driven slides</li>\n<li>style controls for navigation and spacing</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Developer Credits</h3>\n<p>This plugin was developed by ConicPlex, an agency specializing in WordPress plugin development. For more information about ConicPlex and their services, visit <a href=\"https://conicplex.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a>.</p>\n<h3>Credits &amp; 3rd Party Services</h3>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex.com</a></strong>: Carousel Slider for Block Editor uses <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a> (own website) to store plugin insights. Whenever the plugin is activated, deactivated, or uninstalled, an API request is sent to Conicplex to record the action. The API request includes the action, site URL, admin email, plugin version, plugin name, plugin text domain, WordPress version, site language, and site timezone. <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/privacy-policy/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/terms-conditions/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the WordPress admin.</li>\n<li>Insert the <code>Carousel Slider</code> block in the block editor.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"is%20this%20meant%20to%20stay%20lightweight%3F\">\nIs this meant to stay lightweight?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. The goal is to provide a practical slider without unnecessary frontend bloat.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"can%20i%20use%20it%20for%20more%20than%20images%3F\">\nCan I use it for more than images?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. It can be used for content cards, promo sections, testimonials, and similar slide-based layouts.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Build lightweight, accessible carousels with images, cards, and call-to-action slides.",
    "description": "<p>Carousel Slider for Gutenberg Block Editor adds a practical slider block for image carousels, feature slides, marketing sections, and rotating content layouts.</p>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>slide management in the block editor</li>\n<li>responsive slide layouts</li>\n<li>arrows, dots, autoplay, and loop options</li>\n<li>support for image and content-driven slides</li>\n<li>style controls for navigation and spacing</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Developer Credits</h3>\n<p>This plugin was developed by ConicPlex, an agency specializing in WordPress plugin development. For more information about ConicPlex and their services, visit <a href=\"https://conicplex.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a>.</p>\n<h3>Credits &amp; 3rd Party Services</h3>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex.com</a></strong>: Carousel Slider for Block Editor uses <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a> (own website) to store plugin insights. Whenever the plugin is activated, deactivated, or uninstalled, an API request is sent to Conicplex to record the action. The API request includes the action, site URL, admin email, plugin version, plugin name, plugin text domain, WordPress version, site language, and site timezone. <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/privacy-policy/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/terms-conditions/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</p>\n",
